      "authoringHints": {
        "styles": "Every style falls back to the app theme, so set only what the design needs to blend in (its accent, surfaces, borders and text colours), taking colours from the app theme or brand, never the defaults of another product. Radii and sizes are px. Styles are the way to restyle a pack widget: a cssClass only takes effect with workspace Custom styles, and Tailwind class names the pack does not already use are not compiled, so do not rely on either; for a one-off visual a style cannot express, use an Html component. Bind loadingState to the query's isLoading (each widget draws a skeleton or spinner in its own shape); tooltip shows on hover. accentColor colours the focus ring and the calendar's selected days.",
        "validation": "Top-level validation (not properties), each key as {value}: mandatory (\"{{true}}\": a value must be picked, or the checkbox checked) and customRule. customRule fails when it resolves to a non-empty string, which becomes the message: {{components.<name>.value.includes(\"@\") ? \"\" : \"Enter an email\"}}. The message shows under the control after the user leaves it or a surrounding Form tries to submit; components.<name>.isValid and isMandatory are exposed, so gate a submit button with disabledState on them."
      }
    }
